# Backend Rules

- Keep routes and controllers thin.
- Put business logic into services or use-cases.
- Keep database access separate from HTTP handling.
- Validate request body, query, params, and external API responses.
- Use consistent error handling.
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Never expose internal errors or implementation details.
- Enforce authorization on the server.
- Use transactions when multiple writes must be atomic.
- Avoid N+1 database queries.
- Add tests for important business logic and edge cases.
